THOUGHT: Now I understand the vulnerability. Let me analyze `lex_multiline_string`:

```c
static void *lex_multiline_string(struct lexer *lexer)
{
    char *end = (peek(lexer) == '"') ? "\"\"\"" : "'''";

    advance_n(lexer, strlen("'''") - 1);  // advances past 2 chars (the first quote + one more)

    do {
        if (!strncmp(lexer->pos, end, 3)) {
            emit(lexer, LEXEME_STRING);
            lexer->pos += 3;
            return lex_config;
        }
    } while (next(lexer) != '\0');

    return lex_error(lexer, "EOF while scanning multiline string");
}
```

The bug: When the input ends right after the opening `'''` or `"""` with no more characters, `lexer->pos` can go past `lexer->end`. The `next()` function handles this by setting `lexer->pos = lexer->end + 1` and returning `'\0'`. But then `strncmp(lexer->pos, end, 3)` is called with `lexer->pos = lexer->end + 1`, which reads past the buffer boundary.

